.TH NOWAYPROMPT 1 2026-07-26 nowayprompt "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
nowayprompt \- Wayland-native prompt command-line interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nowayprompt
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nowayprompt
shows a configured message or password prompt. It selects Wayland first and
uses the configured TTY fallback only when Wayland is unavailable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --title, --description, --error
Set visible message text.
.TP
.B --prompt
Set password prompt text; requires
.BR --get-pin .
.TP
.B --button-ok, --button-not-ok, --button-cancel
Set button labels.
.TP
.B --wayland-display
Select the Wayland display socket.
.TP
.B --get-pin
Request a password and include it in the result on success.
.TP
.B --json
Write the result as JSON.
.TP
.B --help, -h
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 is OK, 10 is cancellation, 20 is not-OK, and 1 is an error.
.SH FILES
Configuration is looked up inside a single base directory:
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
when set and non-empty, otherwise
.IR $HOME/.config ,
otherwise
.IR /etc .
Within that base,
.I nowayprompt/config.ini
is tried first and
.I wayprompt/config.ini
second; the first candidate that exists is loaded. The
.I wayprompt/config.ini
fallback is consulted silently; candidates are never merged and bases are
never crossed. An existing file that cannot be read or parsed is reported as
an error rather than skipped; if no candidate exists, built-in defaults are
used. See
.BR nowayprompt.conf (5)
for the file format.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pinentry-nowayprompt (1),
.BR nowayprompt-ssh-askpass (1),
.BR nowayprompt.conf (5)
